Last week and this week local officials toured the mobile unit stationed off Interstate 95. Inside an officer watches the vehicles and real time information collected by the equipment. Vehicles' speed is recorded, and a photograph of the driver and license plate is taken if a vehicle exceeds 81 mph. If an officer can match the photo with a driver's license photo, a citation is sent to the home of the person to whom the vehicle is registered.
Ridgeland officials have strongly defended their system, calling it a critical safety measure for the seven-mile stretch through their community.
